"Singularity" by XorDev (Xor)
Source: https://github.com/XorDev/Singularity
Original shader page: https://www.shadertoy.com/view/3csSWB

The shader's header credits three people for golf byte-savings on the
author's code: FabriceNeyret2 (-19), dean_the_coder (-12) and iq (-4).

LICENCE STATEMENT RELIED ON

The repository the shader is published in carries an MIT licence, in its
LICENSE file (https://github.com/XorDev/Singularity/blob/main/LICENSE), which
begins:

    MIT License

    Copyright (c) 2025 Xor

and its README (https://github.com/XorDev/Singularity/blob/main/README.md,
line 2) states:

    "The minified Singularity shader hosted under MIT license"

The sibling file Shaders/twigl-version.glsl in the same repository
(https://github.com/XorDev/Singularity/blob/main/Shaders/twigl-version.glsl,
line 3) is headed "//MIT License". The file this port is made from,
Shaders/shadertoy-version.glsl, has no licence line of its own; it is covered
by the repository's LICENSE and README above. The Shadertoy page itself could
not be read by an automated client (it answers with a bot challenge), so it was
not consulted.

WHAT WAS CHANGED

Ported to Metal Shading Language for MacOS Live Wallpaper. The golfed
declarations were written out as separate statements in the same order
(including the implicit mat2 constructions, the assignment inside the cos()
argument, the zero-initialised accumulator and the post-increment loop test),
the output parameter was declared the way Metal needs it, and time runs at half
the original speed to suit a desktop background (TIME_SCALE in main.metal; set
it to 1.0 for the original pace). The maths, constants and colouring are
untouched. See the note at the top of main.metal.

